This username validator freezes Node on hostile input. Save /workspace/username.mjs:

const RE = /^([a-zA-Z0-9]+[_-]?)+$/;
export function isValidUsername(s) {
  return RE.test(s) && s.length <= 64;
}

First demonstrate the catastrophic backtracking: write username.test.mjs (node:test) that runs isValidUsername('a'.repeat(40) + '!') inside a worker_threads Worker with a 2000ms watchdog that terminates the worker and fails the test if no result arrives. Confirm the hang. Then fix: check length first, and rewrite as a linear pattern such as ^[a-zA-Z0-9]+([_-][a-zA-Z0-9]+)*$ with no nested-quantifier ambiguity. Keep semantics: alphanumeric groups separated by single _ or -, no leading/trailing separator, no doubled separators. Add accept/reject table tests (a, a_b, a-b-c, a__b rejected, _a rejected, a- rejected) and get node --test passing in well under a second.

tools_list = await mcp.list_tools("tools")
for t in tools_list:
    print(t["name"], t["inputSchema"])

